# Useful Git Commands

## Check Repository Status

git status

## View Commit History

git log

## View Short Commit History

git log --oneline

## View All Branches and Commit Graph

git log --oneline --graph --all

## Add Changes

git add .

## Commit Changes

git commit -m "Your commit message"

## Delete a Branch

git branch -d branch-name

## Force Delete a Branch

git branch -D branch-name

---

# Important Points

- Always check `git status` before merging.
- Resolve merge conflicts manually if Git cannot merge automatically.
- Use branches to develop features safely.
- Merge completed features into the main branch.
- Fast-forward merge does not create a separate merge commit.
- Three-way merge usually creates a new merge commit.
- After resolving conflicts, use `git add` and then `git commit`.

